# The exact bytes every figure in README.md was measured on.
#
# `sh scripts/get-data.sh` fetches the first five by accession and checks them
# against this file; `--sim` rebuilds the last two with `dnac mut`. A mismatch
# is a different measurement, not a worse download, and the script stops.
#
# Two of these were not reproducible until 2026-09-17 (docs/batch5.md):
#   o157.fa      is THREE records -- the chromosome and plasmids pOSAK1 and
#                pO157. The script used to fetch only the chromosome.
#   ecoli/w3110  NCBI wraps at 70 columns now and wrapped at 80 then; the
#                script re-wraps to 80, which reproduces the bytes exactly.
#   *_ind.fa     `dnac mut` writes its INPUT'S PATH into the defline, so the
#                argument's spelling is part of the file. See --sim.
